{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i)\n  = n*(n + 1)/2\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "closed", "ucas": "closed sum(i, 1, n, i)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "closed", "loops": [{"loop": "sum(i, 1, n, i)", "closed_form": "n*(n + 1)/2", "accepted": true, "checked": true, "method": ["Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)"]}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "iteration", "points": 101, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "against direct iteration on every point of the domain"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "equals direct iteration on every point of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i)\n  = n*(n + 1)/2\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "closed", "ucas": "closed sum(i, 1, n, i^2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "closed", "loops": [{"loop": "sum(i, 1, n, i^2)", "closed_form": "n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6", "accepted": true, "checked": true, "method": ["Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)"]}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "iteration", "points": 101, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "against direct iteration on every point of the domain"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "equals direct iteration on every point of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i^2)\n  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i^3)\n  = n^2*(n + 1)^2/4\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "closed", "ucas": "closed sum(i, 1, n, i^3)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "closed", "loops": [{"loop": "sum(i, 1, n, i^3)", "closed_form": "n^2*(n + 1)^2/4", "accepted": true, "checked": true, "method": ["Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)"]}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "iteration", "points": 101, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "against direct iteration on every point of the domain"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "equals direct iteration on every point of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i^3)\n  = n^2*(n + 1)^2/4\n  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 0, n, 2^i)\n  = 2^(n + 1) - 1\n  method: geometric\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 62 points of the domain\n  but at 1 points the closed form is undefined (an intermediate leaves the 64-bit range) where iteration is not, e.g. n=62\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "closed", "ucas": "closed sum(i, 0, n, 2^i)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "closed", "loops": [{"loop": "sum(i, 0, n, 2^i)", "closed_form": "2^(n + 1) - 1", "accepted": true, "checked": true, "method": ["geometric"]}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "iteration", "points": 62, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "against direct iteration on every point of the domain"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "equals direct iteration on every point of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 0, n, 2^i)\n  = 2^(n + 1) - 1\n  method: geometric\n  check: equals direct iteration at all 62 points of the domain\n  but at 1 points the closed form is undefined (an intermediate leaves the 64-bit range) where iteration is not, e.g. n=62\n"}, "isError": false}}
